<title>ITALY: De Benedetti's Cofide rises in Milan.</title>
<headline>De Benedetti's Cofide rises in Milan.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Carlo De Benedetti's financial holding company Cofide SpA rose sharply on a weak Milan stock market on Wednesday in higher volumes than seen recently, traders said.</p>
<p>At 1120 GMT, Cofide was quoted 2.91 percent up at a session high so far of 637 lire in volume of nearly four million shares, against a recent daily average of some 1.4 million shares changing hands.</p>
<p>&quot;There's no news that we are aware of but Cofide's been well bought for some time now,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Troubled high-tech group Olivetti was off 1.61 percent at 445 lire.</p>
<p>The all-share Mibtel index was down 0.05 percent.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
